<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Niugini Mining chairman resigns.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Niugini Mining chairman resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Niugini Mining Ltd said on Wednesday it has elected Ian Bayer chairman of the Australia-based resources company following the resignation of R. Dennis O'Connell</p>
<p>Bayer is president and co-chief executive officer of Battle Mountain Gold Company, which holds 50.5 percent of Niugini.</p>
<p>O'Connell earlier this month resigned as chief financial officer of Houston-based Battle Mountain.</p>
<p>Niugini operates gold and copper mines in Chile and Queensland, Australia and holds a 17.5 percent interst in the Lihir gold mine in Papua New Guinea.  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
